        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: AI safety/quality event taxonomy (#82548)",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nImplements a six-family AI safety/quality event taxonomy (#82548) with production emitters at real operational boundaries, plugin API surface, OTEL + Prometheus export, Gateway query API, CLI command, and Control UI dashboard.\n\n## Event families and emission points\n\n| Family | Emitter | Location |\n|--------|---------|----------|\n| \\`prompt_injection.signal\\` | \\`wrapExternalContent()\\` | \\`security/external-content.ts\\` |\n| \\`tool_policy.decision\\` | \\`evaluateTool()\\` | \\`plugins/trusted-tool-policy.ts\\` |\n| \\`memory_context.selected\\` | \\`buildAttemptPrompt()\\` | \\`agents/embedded-agent-runner/run/attempt-prompt-observability.ts\\` |\n| \\`eval.result\\` | \\`runCompactionSafeguard()\\` | \\`agents/agent-hooks/compaction-safeguard.ts\\` |\n| \\`plugin.load\\` | \\`loadPlugin()\\` | \\`plugins/loader.ts\\` |\n| \\`session.boundary\\` | \\`createGatewayStartupTrace()\\` | \\`gateway/server.impl.ts\\` |\n\n## Architectural fixes (commit b55a4334e0b)\n\n**Fix #1:** All safety events route through the single canonical \\`diagnostic-events.ts\\` pipeline. Parallel ad-hoc dispatcher removed.\n\n**Fix #2 — plugin provenance binding:** \\`OpenClawPluginServiceContext\\` exposes \\`safetyDiagnostics.emit()\\`. Emitter is host-stamped at load time with \\`pluginId\\`, \\`origin\\` (bundled vs external), and \\`trusted\\` flag from \\`entry.origin\\`. Plugins cannot self-attest trust.\n\n**Fix #3 — full taxonomy coverage:** All 6 families wired at production boundaries. No hollow stubs.\n\n**Fix #4 — Gateway lifecycle init:** \\`ensureSafetyEventStoreBridge()\\` called in \\`server.impl.ts\\` before \\`createGatewayStartupTrace()\\` and before any RPC handlers load. Boot-phase events no longer dropped.\n\n## Build proof (Kali — 16 cores / 78 GB, commit b55a4334e0b)\n\n\\`\\`\\`\npnpm tsc --noEmit   → 0 errors\npnpm run build      → exit 0\npnpm test           → all suites pass\n\\`\\`\\`\n\nOne pre-existing flaky process-management test (\\`checks-node-compact-small-4\\`) fails intermittently upstream and is unrelated to this PR.",
        "branch": "feat/ai-safety-event-taxonomy",
